{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_operations_metering_doc", "label": "Hosted Usage Metering", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/operations/metering.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_operations_metering_usage_ledger", "label": "Append-Only Tenant-Scoped Usage Ledger", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/operations/metering.md", "source_location": "Metered units", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every entry carries a tenant-bound idempotent usage_id, category, finite positive units, provider cost where applicable, and the exact price-catalog version active when the usage occurred; replaying an identical ID is a no-op while reuse with different semantics fails and alerts. Local guarding is never metered."}, {"id": "docs_operations_metering_reservation_flow", "label": "Reserve/Commit/Release Quota Transaction", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/operations/metering.md", "source_location": "Reservation flow", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Expensive hosted work atomically reserves estimated units before side effects, commits exact usage after durable completion, and releases on cancellation/timeout/failure so a rejected job is never accepted or silently dropped; repair admission checks billing grace before workflow capacity."}, {"id": "docs_operations_metering_metered_units", "label": "Metered Unit Categories", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/operations/metering.md", "source_location": "Metered units", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Seven explicit categories (storage byte-hours, retained events, compute seconds, judge USD, critic USD, browser minutes, repair worker seconds); provider cost and LoopGuard charge are separate fields, and avoided-cost estimates are explanatory,